<root>
	<styles>
		<include src="s2r://panorama/styles/custom_game/hud_shared.vcss_c" />
		<include src="s2r://panorama/styles/custom_game/toasts.vcss_c" />
	</styles>

	<!--
		Toast notifications. 8 placements x 4 slots = 32 toasts.

		NOTHING HERE IS CLICKABLE. hittest="false" on every panel, and the service opens this layout
		with CaptureInput = false. A notification that pulls up a cursor and stops the player aiming
		is worse than no notification.

		STACKING IS THE ROW-POOL TRICK AGAIN. A stack is a flowing column of 4 slots; an unused one
		carries "hidden", which collapses it out of layout entirely. So the service just picks the
		lowest free slot, and when a toast in the middle expires the ones below it close the gap on
		their own with no re-render.

		DRIVEN BY, per toast:
		  t_{place}_{n}         hidden    - free slot, collapsed
		  t_{place}_{n}         show      - on screen; removing it plays the exit transition
		  t_{place}_{n}         color-*   - accent, or none for the neutral card
		  t_{place}_{n}         anim-*    - which direction it enters and leaves from
		  t_{place}_{n}_title   {s:}      - headline
		  t_{place}_{n}_desc    {s:}      - body, blank collapses the line
		  t_{place}_{n}_icon    icon-*    - artwork, or none
		  t_{place}_{n}_bar     dur-*     - how long the progress bar takes to drain
		  t_{place}_{n}_bar     run       - starts it draining

		The root carries "hidden" as authored: a custom_hud_layout shows its layout to EVERY player,
		and per-player state only overlays. Without it, every player on the server sees an empty
		container the moment the entity spawns.
	-->
	<Panel class="hud-screen" hittest="false">
		<Panel id="PanoramaRoot" class="toast-screen hidden" hittest="false">
			<Panel class="toast-stack stack-tl" hittest="false">
				<Panel id="t_tl_0" class="toast hidden" hittest="false">
